      <div type="clause" n="17.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 17.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="504–505" ed="#liebermann"/>Ki en Denelahe franch hume est, s’il ad demi marc vaillant d’aveir champestre, si duinst le den. S<hi rend="italic">eint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.2"/></hi> P<hi rend="italic">iere</hi>; e par le den., que li sire durrad, si erent quite cil ki meindrunt en sun demeine.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="504–505" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui en Denelae francz home est, e il averad demi marc en<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.c"/> argent vailant de aveir<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.8"/> champestre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.9"/>, si devrad duner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.10"/> le dener<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.11"/> Seint Pere; e per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.12"/> le dener, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.13"/> li<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.14"/> seignur durrat, si erent quites<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.15"/> ceals qui meinent en soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.16"/> demaine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.17"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="504–505" ed="#liebermann"/>In Denelahe homo liber qui habuerit catallum campestre ad ualenciam dimidie marce dabit denar. Sancti Petri; et per denarium domini adquietabuntur omnes qui in dominico illius manent.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="260" ed="#robertson"/>Ki en Denelahe franch hume est, s'il ad demi marc vaillant d'aveir champestre, si duinst le den. Seint Piere, e par le den. que li sire durrad si erent quite cil ki meindrunt en sun demeine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="504–505" ed="#liebermann"/>17, 1. Wer im Dänen-Rechtsgebiet ein freier Mann ist, wenn (und <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) er ½ Mark<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de1.c"/> werthes Feldvieh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de.1"/> hat, so soll er den Peterspfennig zahlen; und durch den Pfennig, den der Herr geben soll, werden die, welche auf seiner Domäne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de1.b"/> wohnen, [von Zahlung] frei sein.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">17, 1. Whoever is a free man in the Danish legal district, if (and <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) he has field-cattle worth ½ mark, then he shall pay Peter's Pence; and through the penny which the lord is to give, those who dwell on his demesne shall be free [of payment].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="261" ed="#robertson"/>A free man in the Danelaw who has livestock worth half a mark shall pay Peter's Pence. And by the payment of a penny on the part of a lord, those who live on his demesne land shall be exempt.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="505">ECf 10</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. ebd.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 504–505, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s’. P’. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s’. P’. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wohl Zusatz anglonorm. Zeit zur Unterscheidung von</hi> Mark Gold (6 £)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">probably an addition of the Anglo-Norman period, to distinguish it from the mark of gold (6 £)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">auor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">auor <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ester <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ester <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dinier <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dinier <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">doner <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">doner <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">par <hi rend="italic">Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">par <hi rend="italic">Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">le <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">le Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quietes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quietes <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">504</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">demainne <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> demainer <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">demainne <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> demainer <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">505</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">d. h. auf</hi> inland, <hi rend="italic">das der Herr bewirthschaftet, im Gegensatz zu</hi> Grossguts-Hintersassen auf Bauerhöfen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i.e. on inland, which the lord farms himself, as opposed to the manorial tenants on peasant holdings</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">505</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">80 Pfennig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">80 pence</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_17-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 17{2}. 17a{1}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 17{2}. 17a{1}</seg></note>
